        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T11:12:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TTL_SECONDS_MIN ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 475,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 475,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46c0c6b7_bcc7d9d2",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 64
      },
      "lineNbr": 475,
      "author": {
        "id": 1693933
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-14T10:05:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "setTtlSeconds will be used for representing the TTL in RR received on the wire. So we can throw for values smaller than TTL_SECONDS_MIN",
      "parentUuid": "c5f1d6dc_03ee2b2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 475,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 475,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "baaf3f4e_08d2f08b",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 64
      },
      "lineNbr": 484,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T11:12:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: the first line of each javadoc must be just one line",
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0158b4c3_bfe3ad9c",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 64
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T11:12:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this be an expiration timestamp instead ?\n\nOtherwise, depending on how much processing time passed since we received the advertisement, this will be incorrect. And it may be difficult to use for an application, as they\u0027d need to remember the time at which we sent that value.\n\nAlso, when the reply we send is from cache, this isn\u0027t very useful as it\u0027s the TTL when we received the reply, but it\u0027s actually now lower.\n\nIt may be best to call this \"getAdvertisedTtlSeconds\", and have another method for \"getExpirationTime\" or \"getAdvertisedTime\"; otherwise it sounds like it\u0027s the remaining TTL \"now\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 492,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 492,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b219817_32325d20",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 64
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T11:16:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually to avoid confusion, I\u0027m thinking it\u0027s probably best to only have \"getExpirationTime\" on NsdServiceInfo, and have \"setTtlSeconds\" on the AdvertisingRequest instead",
      "parentUuid": "0158b4c3_bfe3ad9c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 492,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 492,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "beda9a40_29482dd5",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 64
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1693933
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-14T10:05:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Discovery Proxy, TTL value needs to be passed unmodified for long-lived query and DNS Push Notification. See https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8766.html#name-dns-ttl-limiting:\n\n\u003e For received Unicast DNS queries that use LLQ [RFC8764] or DNS Push Notifications [RFC8765], the Multicast DNS record\u0027s TTL SHOULD be returned unmodified, because the notification channel exists to inform the remote client as records come and go. For further details about Long-Lived Queries and its newer replacement, DNS Push Notifications, see Section 5.6.",
      "parentUuid": "3b219817_32325d20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 492,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 492,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
